The evidence separates two questions: synchronous proximal advanced serrated lesions, for which the direct study found no association with distal polyp type, and later serrated lesions, where a distal hyperplastic polyp had an association with subsequent SSLs but not specifically advanced lesions. I’ll record this distinction and review the evidence graph before concluding.

